  "title": "Kueper2024: Unilateral vs bilateral movement-execution EEG dataset",
  "description": "EEG recordings from 8 healthy participants performing self-initiated reaching movements with either the right arm alone (unilateral) or both arms synchronously (bilateral). The data were recorded with a 64-channel wireless active-electrode system and support movement intention recognition for exoskeleton-supported stroke rehabilitation. This BIDS release, generated via MOABB, reformats the originally published Zenodo dataset.",
  "methods_description": "64-channel EEG (Brain Products LiveAmp64, Acticap slim, extended 10-20 montage, 500 Hz, reference FCz, ground AFz) plus 3 misc channels, hardware-filtered 0.1-131 Hz. Each subject performed 3 sets of 40 self-paced movements per condition (unilateral right-arm button press, bilateral both arms), for 6 runs in one session.",
